; status: errors — the same ray listed twice. Both `--h at --(.b .c)` elements
; select the SAME segment (center O to the right edge), a zero-width sector. The
; doubled reflection cancels in the closure product, so without its own guard
; this would pass the count, Kawasaki, and Maekawa checks and emit a
; self-contradictory folded state; the kernel rejects it outright instead.

paper square

--h = map .a onto .d      ; horizontal midline, y = 1/2
--v = map .a onto .b      ; vertical midline, x = 1/2

@collapse --h & --bc and (--h & --bc mountain)
  and --v & --cd and (--v & --ab mountain)
